# The assessment of WF-008 against this build. The requirement identifier is this file's
# stem and appears nowhere inside it, for the reason CHK-003.assessment already states.
#
# WF-008 requires every WorkflowStep contract to declare typed inputs/outputs, side
# effects, idempotency, retry policy, timeout, cacheability/cache key inputs, privileges,
# cancellation behavior, compensation/rollback, determinism class, and evidence emitted.
# OD-WORKFLOW-003 admitted WorkflowStep with exactly these eleven fields, none optional, so
# the Rust type mechanically enforces the declaration for anything that gets constructed.
#
# Partial rather than Met: nothing in this workspace has ever constructed a WorkflowStep.
# The requirement is a constraint on what a real contract declares, and there is no real
# contract yet to check it against -- the same gap OD-WORKFLOW-003 itself names. A verdict
# of Met here would be the vacuous-truth trap OD-CONTRACTS-001's honesty vocabularies exist
# to refuse: "every WorkflowStep declares X" is true of zero WorkflowSteps for the same
# reason it would be true of a million wrong ones.
#
# Not recomputed from the corpus at check time. OD-TRACE-001 records why: CI has no corpus,
# so a guard that read one would be green by being unable to look.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/contracts/nomos-contracts/src/workflow_step.rs#WorkflowStep
gap: docs/records/OD-WORKFLOW-003-workflowstep-is-admitted-to-band-zero-as-wf-008s-declared-contract-not-the-engine.md#a real constructor, publisher, or consumer anywhere in this workspace
